smoltcp: a listener on no address of one IP version

netd listens and binds for IPv4 and IPv6 sockets over one socket set.
Upstream, a TCP listener or a UDP socket on no address takes what comes
to its port in either IP version, so an IPv4 socket on 0.0.0.0 took
IPv6 connections it cannot name, and an IPv4 server and an IPv6-only
one (IPV6_V6ONLY: nginx's `listen [::]:80` beside `listen 80`) could not
share a port: the first socket of the set took both families' traffic.
tcp::Socket::set_listen_version() and udp::Socket::set_ip_version() make
such a socket take one version only. Unchanged without them. With tests.
Derived from smoltcp, so under smoltcp's license (0BSD).

